    | [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'To demonstrate fundamental quantum logic, we will create a Bell state (a maximally entangled state) using a Hadamard gate and a CNOT gate.\n\n### Technical Explanation of the Gates\n1.  **Hadamard (H) Gate:** This gate maps the basis state $|0\\rangle$ to the superposition state $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. It effectively places the qubit into a state of equal probability of being measured as 0 or 1.\n2.  **CNOT (Controlled-NOT) Gate:** This is a two-qubit gate. If the control qubit (qubit 0) is $|1\\rangle$, it flips the state of the target qubit (qubit 1). By applying this to a qubit in superposition, we create **entanglement**, where the state of the two qubits becomes inseparable.\n\n### Python Code (Qiskit)\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, transpile\nfrom qiskit_aer import AerSimulator\n\n# Initialize a circuit with 2 qubits and 2 classical bits\n# Qubits are initialized to |00>\ncircuit = QuantumCircuit(2, 2)\n\n# Apply Hadamard gate to qubit 0\n# State becomes (|00> + |10>) / sqrt(2)\ncircuit.h(0)\n\n# Apply CNOT gate (control=0, target=1)\n# State becomes (|00> + |11>) / sqrt(2) (Bell State)\ncircuit.cx(0, 1)\n\n# Measure both qubits into the classical bits\ncircuit.measure([0, 1], [0, 1])\n\n# Execute on a local simulator\nsimulator = AerSimulator()\ncompiled_circuit = transpile(circuit, simulator)\njob = simulator.run(compiled_circuit, shots=1024)\nresult = job.result()\n\n# Extract and display the results\ncounts = result.get_counts(circuit)\nprint(f"Simulation counts: {counts}")\n```\n\n### Expected Output/Results\nBecause the circuit creates the state $\\frac{|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$, the qubits are perfectly correlated. When you measure the circuit, you will observe either `00` or `11` with approximately equal frequency (50% each), but you will **never** observe `01` or `10`.\n\n**Typical output:**\n`Simulation counts: {\'00\': 512, \'11\': 512}`\n*(Note: Minor variations occur due to the probabilistic nature of quantum measurement across 1,024 shots.)*', 'extras': {'signature': 'EjQKMgEMOdbHm1VPrZASxAvaCDkYYa3Pg2010l/3L4gPO48+WBLD8M/AT/2HGKyCGBmgSZHy'}}]
